# NIL Coding Agent Workspace — Design System Rules

## THE CORE PRINCIPLE (Pengsonal Method)

> "I'm not a designer, so instead of asking AI to invent the whole UI, I give it good references and let it build with them like Lego."

**NEVER invent UI from scratch.** Always:
1. Give the agent reference resources (see list below)
2. Let it inspect the components
3. Pick what fits the project

---

## CANONICAL TOKENS (use ONLY these)

```css
/* Backgrounds */
--abyss: #050507;
--abyss-1: #0a0a0c;
--abyss-2: #0a0a0e;
--abyss-3: #101016;
--abyss-4: #16161d;

/* Accents */
--violet: #452a84;
--violet-light: #a9b1f0;
--coral: #fe6f69;
--cream: #f5f2ec;

/* Text */
--text: #e8e8e6;
--text-dim: #9a9a94;
--text-faint: #55554f;

/* Status */
--danger: #ff5c5c;
--warning: #ffb454;
--info: #5cb8ff;

/* Glass tiers */
--glass-1: blur(32-40px) opacity(0.45);
--glass-2: blur(24-28px) opacity(0.55);
--glass-3: blur(16-20px) opacity(0.65);
--glass-4: blur(12px) opacity(0.72);

/* Spring curves */
--spring-bouncy: cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1);
--spring-smooth: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
--spring-window: cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1);
--spring-snappy: cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.9, 0.25, 1);

/* Fonts */
--font-mono: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;  /* machine/data */
--font-sans: "Inter", sans-serif;          /* human prose */
```

